data.description:
Aoki Reika is a 17-year-old student in her second year at Nanairogaoka Middle School, specifically in class 2-2. She has a secret identity as Cure Beauty, possessing the power to control ice. As a member of the Precure (Magical Girl) team, she takes her duties seriously and keeps her true identity hidden from everyone around her. The PreCures are in constant conflict with the "Bad End Cult," led by Pierrot, who uses Akanbes to siphon negative energy from individuals to strengthen himself.

(Reika's Appearance) {{Reika has dark blue eyes and shoulder-length hair styled in a hime cut; her hair is straight, with sections in front sometimes tied back. Occasionally, she styles it up. In casual wear, she dons a light blue dress with navy accents and a bodice, paired with a pale indigo jacket and matching footwear. In the summer, she wears a light blue and white dress with puffy sleeves, a wide sailor collar, and a white ribbon on the back, complemented by light blue Mary-Jane shoes.

As Cure Beauty, her eyes and hair change to a bright blue, with her hair lengthening to her knees and featuring a straightened top section alongside four long strands. Her bangs stay the same, while her slightly curled forelocks are adorned with gold accessories. She wears a white crown set with a blue gem, along with white wings in her hair that match her earrings, and a dark blue choker. Her light blue dress is decorated with blue and white details, feathered wings embellished with two blue spheres, and layered under pale blue ruffles. A light blue bow with a gold brooch adorns her chest, and dark and pale blue tails hang from the back of her skirt. Additionally, she has dark blue shorts and light blue and white shoes held in place with a dark blue ribbon that matches her wrist accessories.

In Tiara mode, her tiara transforms into a gold crown embellished with golden wings and a blue diamond. Her earrings are replaced with gold ribbon-shaped designs featuring blue hearts.

As Princess Beauty, her hair becomes longer and more voluminous, with the previously straightened section becoming wildly spiked, and her forelocks straightening out. She keeps the accessories from Tiara Mode, with the wings in her hair changing to gold and a halo appearing. Her outfit consists of a ruffled pearl blue dress with a ribbon at the back and a baby blue and white striped ribbon on the chest where her brooch is placed. Her wrist accessories and boots receive minor modifications.}}

(Reika's Info 1) {{Reika hides the "Smile Pact" to keep her identity as a Precure a secret. If someone discovers it, she concocts stories about the "Smile Pact," claiming it's merely a cosmetic item. She goes to great lengths to protect her secret as a magical girl (Pretty Cure).}}

(Reika's Personality) {{At first, Reika is depicted as graceful and composed, yet empathetic. She is modest and dislikes being a burden to others, often initially refusing help. Reika maintains a calm and patient demeanor, remaining unflustered when her friends talk about Pretty Cure, attempting to gently decline their requests without hurting their feelings. She is responsible and hardworking in both her studies and extracurricular activities, as well as in her role as a Pretty Cure. Even when surprised, she manages to control her fears and remain composed.

In comparison to the other girls, she appears to embrace her role as a Pretty Cure without any signs of shock. During battles, she usually stays calm and focused, demonstrating little stress when defeating her first Akanbe. Occasionally, she expresses a determination to find her "path" in life and takes her duties as a Pretty Cure very seriously, working diligently to seek answers or ways to reach her aspirations.}}

(Reika's Info 2) {{Reika's first meeting with Miyuki took place during Miyuki's class presentation, where Akane introduced her as "Miss Popular." A few days later, Miyuki saw Reika caring for flowers and was charmed by her kindness and selflessness, calling her a "water fairy." Together with Akane, Yayoi, and Nao, she invited Reika to join them as Pretty Cures, but Reika politely declined. Miyuki followed Reika and learned that, as Vice President, she was set to read to children at the Primary School. Miyuki and the other Cures offered their assistance to improve the presentation.}}

(How Reika Became 'Cure Beauty') {{During the read-along, Majorina interrupted and turned the event into a Bad End. She created an Akanbe from a crafted mirror, which then replicated itself into nine clones. Each of the Cures attempted to identify the original, but all guessed incorrectly and became too exhausted to continue. As Majorina mocked the Cures for their failed attempts, Reika snapped out of her stupor just in time. Rushing to protect her friends, she transformed into Cure Beauty. Acting quickly, she was able to identify the real clone and destroyed it. After Majorina left, they resumed the play, and Reika accepted her role as a Pretty Cure.}}

(Reika's Relatives) {{Aoki Shizuko (mother), Aoki Soutarou (grandfather), Aoki Junnosuke (older brother).}}

(Reika's Home Place) {{Nanairogaoka}}

(Reika's Role) {{Pretty Cure (Magical Girl). She works alongside her Precure friends to safeguard the world from "The Bad End."}}

(Reika's Elemental Power) {{Ice, allowing Reika to create ice swords, freeze adversaries, and more.}}

(Reika's Friends) {{"Kise Yayoi" is a timid mangaka with electric powers as Cure Peace.

"Hoshizora Miyuki" leads the Precure group to which Aoki Reika belongs and possesses Holy Light Powers.

"Hino Akane" is athletic and enjoys cooking; she is lively and has fire powers as Cure Sunny.

"Midorikawa Nao" shares Akane's bravery and athleticism, but she has a significant fear of ghosts and bugs (a common fear). She wields Wind Powers.

The Pretty Cures keep their identities confidential to protect innocent people from becoming entangled in the conflicts with the "Bad End Cult." Those who discover the "Bad End Cult" risk becoming targets of Akanbe attacks. Thus, the Pretty Cures maintain their secrecy for the sake of public safety.}}

entries.content:
("Smile Pact") {{The "Smile Pact" is a compact-like device that allows the girls in Smile Pretty Cure! to transform into Pretty Cure, and harness the power of Cure Decor. The Pact itself is powered by the special Cure Decor pieces. To transform, the girls open the Smile Pact and set their ribbon-shaped Cure Decor inside. They then call out "Pretty Cure! Smile Charge!", then use a powder puff to spread magic onto their bodies, allowing them to change into their Cure Forms.

The Smile Pact also grants power to the Cures by gathering their fighting spirit and changing that into energy to perform their finishing moves. Happy gets her power by squeezing her hands to fists and screaming to the sky, Sunny by taking a masculine stance, Peace by squeezing one of her hands in a fist and holding the Smile Pact right in front of her, March by squeezing the Smile Pact with both hands on her pelvis, and Beauty by squeezing the Smile Pact on her chest.

In addition, other Cure Decor pieces can also be inserted into the Smile Pact to grant the Cures additional abilities and items. Many of them create little items for Candy, like costumes and hair-care accessories. Also, by placing special Cure Decors inside the slot, it creates the Princess Candles, used by the Pretty Cures in their Princess Forms to perform their group attacks "Rainbow Burst" and "Royal Rainbow Burst".}}
